    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0139" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg37"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.51A/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>)<anchor n="32"
                        xml:id="d49-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-24T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 24, 1919, 6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>On recommendation Secretary Treasury, President has designated Monday, January
                    12, 1920 for convening of second Pan American Financial Conference, authorized
                    in diplomatic and consular Act, March 3rd, 1917,<anchor n="33" xml:id="d49-f2"/>
                    and hopes this date will be agreeable to Government of Brazil. Act limits
                    official delegation to three members. Please convey to government to which you
                    are accredited formal invitation to participate.</p>
                <p>Confidential for your guidance. Most important factor in Financial Conference is
                    conference between Secretary of Treasury and respective Ministers of Finance.
                    Secretary of Treasury, therefore, most anxious that Minister of Finance head
                    delegation and that delegation include persons prominent in banking and
                    commerce. Department believes that it would be desirable for you to convey the
                    Secretary of Treasury’s hopes regarding the personnel of the delegations orally
                    and unofficially at the same time that you transmit the formal and written
                    invitation for participation in the Conference. Cable reply.<anchor n="34"
                        xml:id="d49-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d49-f1" n="32" type="source" xml:id="d49-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, May 24, to the
                    diplomatic representatives in all other Latin American countries.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d49-f2" n="33" xml:id="d49-f2-content">
                <p>39 Stat. 1052.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d49-f3" n="34" xml:id="d49-f3-content">
                <p>Acceptances received from all governments addressed; not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
